<pdd-reason>Preserve filesystem navigation, independent sorting, safe path copying, and durable personal places for the approved Ubuntu story.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"location","signature":"(text: &str, current: &Path) -> io::Result<PathBuf>"},{"name":"entries","signature":"(path: &Path) -> io::Result<Vec<Entry>>"},{"name":"sort_entries","signature":"(items: &mut [Entry], key: Sort, descending: bool)"},{"name":"clipboard_text","signature":"(paths: &[PathBuf], shell: bool) -> String"},{"name":"home","signature":"() -> PathBuf"},{"name":"size_label","signature":"(bytes: Option<u64>) -> String"},{"name":"shell_quote","signature":"(value: &str) -> String"}]}}
</pdd-interface>
Implement src/core.rs in Rust 2021 using std, serde, and serde_json. GTK MUST NOT be needed for this module's behavior.
<contract_rules>
R1 - Resolve absolute, tilde/home, and relative input against the displayed folder. Normalize dot components without canonicalizing symlinks. Preserve spaces and Unicode. Empty paths are errors. MUST NOT execute path input, expand shell commands, or change source files.
R2 - List direct children including dotfiles, dotfolders, symlinks, and broken symlinks. Failed metadata on one entry must not hide that entry. Expose path, folder flag, optional byte size, modification timestamp and symlink flag. Do not recursively calculate folder totals. Unreadable/missing directories return an error without changing favorites or current location.
R3 - Sort by exactly Name, Modified, Size, each ascending or descending. Folders remain first in both directions. Ties are deterministic. Name comparisons ignore case.
R4 - Copy absolute paths as plain strings (newline-separated for multiple selection) or separately shell-quote each path for a POSIX terminal (space-separated). Apostrophes, spaces, dollar signs, newlines and command syntax MUST round-trip literally. Copying MUST NOT execute anything.
R5 - Preferences use $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/personal-files/preferences.json, falling back to ~/.config. Remember favorites, visits with count and last timestamp, last successful folder, sort direction/key, theme and chosen image; ordered saved tabs with absolute paths, independent sort/direction and active-tab index. Load legacy preferences without tabs. Sanitize relative saved tab paths and clamp the active index while preserving otherwise valid favorites/history. Read compatible JSON preferences from the temporary Python reference. Favorites remain explicit and deduplicated; visits automatically populate Recent/Frequent separately. Missing favorites remain visible for disconnected mounts. Never silently promote or evict a manual favorite.
R6 - Bound visit history to the newest 200 unique folders; Recent ranks newest first and Frequent ranks count then recency. Refresh must not count as a visit (enforced by caller). Manual favorites are outside this bound. Clearing visits must retain favorites.
R7 - Save atomically with a same-directory temporary file, private 0600 mode, fsync then rename. Do not truncate the existing file before a successful replacement. Invalid JSON or schema must load defaults with a visible warning; preserve the corrupt original as a timestamped backup before saving recovery. Temporary files must be cleaned on error. Surface persistence errors.
</contract_rules>
Acceptance oracle: user_stories/story__personal_places.md and tests/acceptance.rs. Do not weaken either to accommodate implementation drift.
